# Every text file checks out LF, as it is stored (HF-126, decided in the cut of 2026-11-02). Measured: of 821 text files none holds a
# CR in the index, and 162 sat CRLF on disk because core.autocrlf rewrote them at checkout -- so a fresh clone read `n/tontine.n`
# with 440 CRs and stage 20 counted a fragment holding a newline as absent, and the forge's grammars (written LF) showed as modified
# in every status. With this rule a checkout is LF whatever the machine's setting; a court reading its own sources by byte offset
# reads the bytes git holds.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party sources check out BYTE-EXACT, never converted: their SHA256SUMS are claims about those bytes (Ring++ found
# core.autocrlf rewriting the grammar's 21 MB parser.c on checkout, so the copy no longer matched its release).
vm/vendor/** -text
